==English==
{{wikipedia}}
{{was wotd|2011|December|12}}

===Etymology===
From {{term|devil|devil's|lang=en}} {{term|advocate|lang=en}}, a calque of {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|advocatus diaboli|advocātus diabolī|the devil’s advocate|lang=la}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[devil]]’s [[advocate]]|pl=[[devil's advocates|devil’s advocates]]}}

# {{context|idiomatic|lang=en}} One who [[debate]]s from a view which he or she may not actually hold, usually to determine its [[validity]] or simply for the sake of [[argument]].
# {{qualifier|Roman Catholic Church}} A [[canon]] lawyer appointed by the [[church|Church]] to argue against the canonization of the proposed [[candidate]].

